      "content": "You are on the right track; these \"ghostly\" resonances are fundamentally mathematical side effects stemming from the instrument's physical geometry, like how a specific hollowed-out pipe resonates at certain points. They are the acoustic equivalent of the natural imperfections in a perfectly engineered system. And yes, they absolutely can produce sounds that feel intentional, adding a unique *personality* or texture—a subtle grit, a waver, or a specific coloration—that the player isn't consciously creating with their embouchure or breath pressure. This is where the raw, unpredictable beauty of acoustics meets the art of performance.",
